{"sections": [
  {"key": "arc", "title": "The arc", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue compounded at 34.8% a year from $404.5 million in FY2016 to $5.93 billion in FY2025 [F1][F10][F196]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Growth was front-loaded: 64.2% in FY2021, then 11.8% in FY2022 and 0.1% in FY2023, before recovering to 16.4% in FY2024 and 10.6% in FY2025 [D218][D263][D311][D358][D406]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2017 operating loss of $3.49 billion was driven by a $2.6 billion increase in stock-based compensation, primarily the CEO award and IPO-related RSUs [F12][P74]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The operating margin has improved every year since FY2017, from -422.5% to -9.0% in FY2025, a 5.7pp gain in the latest year alone [F22][F30][D419]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "North America remains the largest geography at 58.6% of FY2025 revenue but contributed only 4.4pp of the 10.6% growth [D456][D458][D406]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Other revenue grew 62.9% in FY2025 and contributed 5.4pp, nearly matching advertising's 5.3pp contribution on 5.8% growth [D544][D545][D537][D538]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Advertising growth came from roughly 17% more impressions, largely via Sponsored Snaps and Spotlight, partly offset by a 10% lower cost per impression; other revenue rose on subscription growth [P24]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating costs grew 5.1% against 10.6% revenue growth in FY2025, an incremental operating margin of 44.8% [D423][D406][D429]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The diluted share count rose 2.1% in FY2025, so the 35.7% smaller loss per share trailed the 34.0% smaller net loss [D425][D409][D408]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "margins", "title": "Margins and costs", "sentences": [
